#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111891 :tutorial/content "Suppose that we have a cube whose edges are $2\\,\\textrm{cm}$ in length, like the one shown below. \n\n![](images/b9/b974b6e782801fbe2099971afd0df9a5c6e05a10afc2ce0e4054c850088e753b.png)\n\nThe formula for the volume $V$ of a cube with sides of length $s$ is given by\n\n$$\nV = s^3.\n$$\n\nTo find the volume of this cube, we substitute $s=2 \\: \\textrm{cm}$ into the formula. This gives\n\n$$\nV = (2\\, \\textrm{cm})^3 = 8 \\text{ cm}^3 .\n$$\n\nSo the volume of the cube is $8\\,\\textrm{cm}^3.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "7ebfe2f1-6dce-5f67-bf2d-58fcd1660014" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4348 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
